  "description": "2025 Cadillac Lyriq (GM Ultium) diagnostics. 29-bit CAN (ISO 15765-4, ATSP7). Confirmed on-vehicle: pack voltage, module voltages, and battery temperatures on ECUs 40 & 1D. SOC/cell-voltage DIDs (ECU CB, from OBDb) have derived formulas but ECU CB does not answer via a single-bus ELM327 clone. See docs/lyriq-did-map.md.",
  "provenance": {
    "derivedFrom": "Live 2025 Lyriq (VIN 1GYKPTRL5SZ302606) via a Pi BLE bridge + Viecar ELM327 clone, cross-referenced with the community OBDb/Cadillac-LYRIQ database. See docs/lyriq-re-log.md and docs/lyriq-did-map.md.",
    "confidence": "CONFIRMED on-vehicle: protocol, ECU map, pack voltage (1D.33E5 x2.7), module voltages (40.416C-E /100), temps (40.4127/4124/40E5/40E6 /32, 40.434F -40). SOC/cell-V formulas derived from OBDb but ECU CB unreachable on our adapter (likely separate CAN bus). Pack current still unknown.",
    "license": "Battery signals cross-referenced with OBDb/Cadillac-LYRIQ (CC BY-SA). J1979 signals are public-domain."
  },
  "protocol": {
    "canFormat": "29bit",
    "obdProtocol": 7,
    "note": "CONFIRMED on-vehicle: ISO 15765-4 CAN 29-bit/500k, force with ATSP7 (auto-detect ATSP0 FAILS on the Lyriq). Battery/propulsion controller (BECM) is ECU 40: request header 18DA40F1, response filter 18DAF140. A Viecar ELM327 clone DID handle 29-bit multiframe here, though an STN adapter (OBDLink CX/MX+) is still recommended for reliability."
  },
